  [1mSection 4 — Error handling[0m

  - [1mCorrupt or unparseable [38;5;153mlocalStorage[0m — [38;5;153mstorage.js[39m catches, does not throw into the app, and returns empty state while
    preserving the bad value under a [38;5;153m…:corrupt-<timestamp>[39m key rather than overwriting it. Silent data loss is the
    worse failure here.
  - [1m[38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m unavailable or quota exceeded[0m (private mode, full disk) — the app runs in memory and shows a persistent
    "changes won't be saved" banner. It does not crash, and it does not pretend to save.
  - [1mSchema version mismatch[0m — state carries [38;5;153mversion: 1[39m. An unknown version is treated as corrupt, per the first rule.
  - [1mInvalid [38;5;153mdueAt[0m — a date that doesn't parse is normalized to [38;5;153mnull[39m on read, so a bad value degrades to "no due date"
    instead of producing [38;5;153mNaN[39m comparisons that would silently make [38;5;153mdueState[39m return [38;5;153mok[39m forever.

  [1mSection 5 — Testing[0m

  [38;5;153mdue-state.js[39m is where the tests earn their keep, and it's testable without a DOM or a fake clock because [38;5;153mnow[39m is a
  parameter. Cases: each threshold boundary (just before, exactly at, just after), [38;5;153mdueAt: null[39m, completed-with-past-due,
  ack matching [38;5;153mforDueAt[39m, ack orphaned by a changed [38;5;153mforDueAt[39m, and the two thresholds dismissed independently.

  [38;5;153mtasks.js[39m and [38;5;153mstorage.js[39m get unit tests too — storage's corruption path especially, since it's the one that protects
  data. [38;5;153mui.js[39m I'd leave untested at this scale; DOM assertions on a five-element render cost more to maintain than they
  catch.

  [1mTooling[0m

  No tooling is configured yet, and it's cheapest to set up before any code exists. My recommendation is the first two
  only — linting/formatting and unit tests. E2E infrastructure for a single page with no network and no auth is
  machinery you'd maintain for very little signal, and mutation testing is premature before the code exists.
